1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,157
This $5 coffee

2
00:00:01,157 --> 00:00:03,276
could end up costing $40.

3
00:00:03,276 --> 00:00:05,005
Not because of the café.

4
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,655
Because of your bank.

5
00:00:06,655 --> 00:00:08,805
Imagine you have $100.

6
00:00:08,805 --> 00:00:10,291
You buy coffee for $5,

7
00:00:10,291 --> 00:00:11,557
lunch for $12,

8
00:00:11,557 --> 00:00:13,136
gas for $28,

9
00:00:13,136 --> 00:00:15,324
and groceries for $90.

10
00:00:15,324 --> 00:00:16,706
That’s $35 more

11
00:00:16,706 --> 00:00:18,360
than you have.

12
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,403
Process those purchases in order,

13
00:00:20,403 --> 00:00:23,583
and only the last one causes an overdraft.

14
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:24,698
But Wells Fargo used

15
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:26,959
to do something different.

16
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:29,906
It processed the biggest purchases first.

17
00:00:29,906 --> 00:00:31,821
Groceries: $90.

18
00:00:31,821 --> 00:00:32,953
$10 left.

19
00:00:32,953 --> 00:00:34,453
Gas? Overdraft.

20
00:00:34,453 --> 00:00:36,193
Lunch? Another.

21
00:00:36,193 --> 00:00:37,790
And that $5 coffee?

22
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:38,883
One more.

23
00:00:38,883 --> 00:00:39,928
Same purchases.

24
00:00:39,928 --> 00:00:41,312
Same amount spent.

25
00:00:41,312 --> 00:00:43,791
But THREE overdraft fees instead of one.

26
00:00:43,791 --> 00:00:45,358
At $35 per fee,

27
00:00:45,358 --> 00:00:48,267
that’s $105 in charges.

28
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:49,625
And that $5 coffee

29
00:00:49,625 --> 00:00:52,368
gets its own $35 fee.

30
00:00:52,368 --> 00:00:54,626
$5 becomes $40.

31
00:00:54,626 --> 00:00:56,263
Court records describe a customer

32
00:00:56,263 --> 00:00:58,864
who went just $120 over

33
00:00:58,864 --> 00:01:02,914
and incurred $506 in fees.

34
00:01:02,914 --> 00:01:04,284
After years of appeals,

35
00:01:04,284 --> 00:01:09,255
a $203 million restitution award was upheld in the case.

36
00:01:09,255 --> 00:01:11,784
This was Wells Fargo’s old system.

37
00:01:11,784 --> 00:01:13,938
The coffee was still $5.

38
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:17,170
The bank just made the order more expensive.
